# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Anything prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ ships to
# the client — keep secrets out of NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars.

# Auis dot — the floating shortcut menu in the bottom-right corner (Review /
# Edit / State modes, the Agents panel). Hide it without disabling the shortcuts:
#NEXT_PUBLIC_AUIS_DOT_DISABLED=true

# Review Bridge — serverless, embedded in the Next app (/api/review-bridge/*),
# persisted to review-bridge/data/*.json. `npm run dev` already brings it up:
# no server, no port, no token.
#
# Optional: a shared secret for agents calling the bridge from outside the
# browser (the skills, the mention runner). Requests carrying it in the
# `x-bridge-agent-token` header are treated as an agent session. Only matters
# once you put Auis behind an auth layer (see app/api/review-bridge/_session.ts).
#BRIDGE_AGENT_TOKEN=
#
# Optional: where the bridge keeps its pre-write snapshots
# (default: ~/.auis/review-bridge-backups).
#REVIEW_BRIDGE_BACKUP_DIR=

# Mention trigger (LOCAL DEV ONLY). With this on, writing "@Claude …" or
# "@Grok …" in a Review Mode pin or reply opens that agent's CLI right away,
# from the route that stored the comment (app/api/review-bridge/_mention.ts) —
# no loop, nothing polling. It fires only for YOUR writes (admin role), never
# for a write authored by an agent, only on creation, never in production, and
# only for an agent switched on in the Auis dot's Agents panel. What the run
# does is scripts/mention-prompt.md; scripts/mention-run.mjs supervises it
# (one editor at a time behind a working-tree lock in ~/.auis, failure reply in
# the thread). Dry run: `npm run mention:dry -- <commentId> claude`.
#AUIS_MENTION_TRIGGER=1
#
# The runner hands the agents only a basic environment (PATH, HOME, locale…):
# app secrets and API keys stay out, and each CLI uses the account it is logged
# into. Binaries outside the PATH (the runner also looks in ~/.local/bin):
#CLAUDE_BIN=/path/to/claude
#GROK_BIN=/path/to/grok
#
# @Grok answers through Grok Build (xAI's official CLI): install it, run
# `grok login` and check `grok version` — verified with Grok Build 1.0.41
# (flags, `grok models`, both ceilings). XAI_API_KEY, if set, goes only to Grok
# and bills per token. Grok has no per-run spend ceiling like Claude's
# --max-budget-usd — only the watchdog (10 min in Reply, 30 min in Edit).
#XAI_API_KEY=
#
# Per-run spend ceiling handed to `claude -p --max-budget-usd` (default 5).
#MENTION_MAX_USD=5

# Review Mode — voice transcription and comment suggestions (OpenAI). Used only
# on the server by /api/review/transcribe and /api/review/suggest; it is never
# exposed to the browser. Without it, voice and suggestion actions stay hidden
# while the rest of Review Mode continues to work.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
